#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "665a164d-a4b1-5104-b010-c9d2e4fb6aae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228180} {:answer-field/id #uuid "74529953-db83-50c9-b0ad-3787b4203c7b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228181}] :question/id #uuid "5195016b-d389-5c7b-a222-3fb5f86b99aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-334540" :question/problem "$x^{′}(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x + \\begin{bmatrix}e^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, x(0) = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: $e^{At} = \\begin{bmatrix}e^{2t} & te^{2t} \\\\ 0 & e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}$, where $A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$.*\n\n| $x(t) =$ |  | $2te^{2t}$ |  | $+ \\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{t}$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $ds$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $0$ |  |  |  |  |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "237ca5ab-34cd-58e7-9713-b55a6e87c11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "237ca5ab-34cd-58e7-9713-b55a6e87c11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305489} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dd60399-b452-5b9e-ab6f-1b2c49d47ce4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307619} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "752cf0f7-34a2-5108-a051-4523e28c9195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{5(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "752cf0f7-34a2-5108-a051-4523e28c9195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{5(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306265} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d548ec-0d73-5a36-8fa4-84091d6ec494" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cc8319e7-c74a-546c-ac46-138a893fec53" :question/math-academy-id "q-334848" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(1)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5s} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29953a21-209b-586e-a213-f4a4fa9d67d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29953a21-209b-586e-a213-f4a4fa9d67d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305546} :answer-field/id #uuid "af02c77a-cb82-5db7-8040-47a534b70764" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47fdaa8b-a137-5a55-9e2b-f6799e375b7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-335081" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
